From 4d8dc61995e34da59ee806c4862558da28b2329b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomasz Maciej Nowak <tmn505@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Sep 2025 22:00:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ipq806x: add Mojo/Arista C-130

Mojo/Arista Networks C-130 is a dual-band tri-radio access point,
also sold by WatchGuard under name AP420.

Specification
SoC: Qualcomm Atheros IPQ8068
RAM: 512 MiB DDR3L
Flash: 32 MiB SPI NOR
       128 MiB Parallel NAND
WiFi: 2.4 GHz 4T4R QCA9994 connected to PCIe lanes
      5 GHz 4T4R QCA9994 connected to PCIe lanes
      2.4/5 GHz 2T2R QCA9882 standard size miniPCIe card
Ethernet: 2x 10/100/1000 Mbps AR8033
          port labeled Poe+ accepts 802.3af/at as power source
LEDs: 1x GPIO controlled
Buttons: 1x GPIO controlled
USB: 1x 3.0
Serial: 1x RJ45, Cisco pinout
        baud: 115200, parity: none, flow control: none

OpenWrt is written to the primary NAND slot (the first 64 MiB, as one
UBI); the OEM system in the second slot stays as it is.

[port: carried unchanged in code from github.com/tmn505/openwrt, branch
 watchguard, commit 4d8dc61995e3; the message is shortened here, the
 original has the by-hand installation and the USB power notes]

Signed-off-by: Tomasz Maciej Nowak <tmn505@gmail.com>
